{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:6121339 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:6121339 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"6121339","source":"MED","pmid":"6121339","doi":"10.1098/rstb.1981.0178","title":"Determining steps in the regulatory GTPase cycle of rat pancreatic adenylate cyclase.","authorString":"Christophe J, Svoboda M, Lambert M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Christophe J","lastName":"Christophe","firstName":"J","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Svoboda M","lastName":"Svoboda","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Lambert M","lastName":"Lambert","firstName":"M","initials":"M"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1080","volume":"296","journalIssueId":463213,"dateOfPublication":"1981 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":1981,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Philos Trans R Soc Lond B Biol Sci","title":"Philosophical transactions of the Royal Society of London. Series B, Biological sciences","essn":"1471-2970","issn":"0962-8436","isoabbreviation":"Philos Trans R Soc Lond B Biol Sci","nlmid":"7503623"},"printPublicationDate":"1981-12-01"},"pubYear":"1981","pageInfo":"139-150","abstractText":"The time course of activation and deactivation and the degree of activation at steady state [Ea]/[Etot] of adenylate cyclase, in semi-purified rate pancreatic plasma membranes, were compatible with a simple two-state model with three rate constants, so that [Ea]/[Etot] = k+1/(k+1 + k2 + k-1). The hormone CCK-8 increased k+1 with GTP in a dose-dependent manner, from 0.2 to 10.9 min-1; k-1 increased from 0.01 to 0.3 min-1, i.e. in proportion, but k2 was unaltered at 7 min-1, so that [Ea]/[Etot] increased 15-fold, from 4 to 61%. A similar activation was obtained after cholera toxin pretreatment by a different mechanism. The toxin pretreatment exerted a major inhibitory effect on the value of k2 and on the corresponding GTPase activity. A pretreatment at the high cholera toxin concentration (10 micrograms/ml) exerted two additional effects that became evident when p[NH]ppG rather than GTP was used as activating nucleotide: (a) a relatively large increase in k-1 from an unmeasurably low control value to 0.3 min-1, and (b) a four-fold increase in the p[NH]ppG activation rate, k+1. This contrasted with the action of CCK-8, which increased k-1 and k+1 in proportion.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pancreas","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cell Membrane","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Rats"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cholecystokinin","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"GTP Phosphohydrolases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Phosphoric Monoester Hydrolases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cholera Toxin","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Guanine Nucleotides","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Enzyme Activation","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Kinetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adenylyl Cyclases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Cholecystokinin","registryNumber":"9011-97-6"},{"name":"Cholera Toxin","registryNumber":"9012-63-9"},{"name":"Guanine Nucleotides","registryNumber":"0"},{"name":"GTP Phosphohydrolases","registryNumber":"EC 3.6.1.-"},{"name":"Adenylyl Cyclases","registryNumber":"EC 4.6.1.1"},{"name":"Phosphoric Monoester Hydrolases","registryNumber":"EC 3.1.3.2"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0178"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":2,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"1982-05-12","dateOfCreation":"1981-12-18","dateOfRevision":"2018-12-12","firstPublicationDate":"1981-12-01","firstIndexDate":"2008-01-29","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}